  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Friday...\n\nA cold front will move through the region this morning. The latest\nHiRes models are showing a few showers developing north and east\nof Billings before sunrise. Precipitation totals are not expected\nto be high, with up to a few hundredths of an inch forecast. \nOtherwise, breezy winds from the northwest will accompany the \nfront through this morning. Winds gusting in the teens and 20s \n(greatest in southeastern Montana) mph will continue through much \nof the afternoon. Temperatures will cool a bit today, with highs \nforecast to be in the 60s to low 70sF.\n\nOtherwise, ridging will dominate the forecast through next week.\nThis will bring above normal temperatures and dry conditions. High\ntemperatures will be in the 70s to low 80s Sunday and 80s to near\n90F on Monday. The latest probability for a high temperature of at\nleast 90F on Monday is 25-50% (greatest in the river valleys \nsouth and east of Billings). A few climate sites may approach \ntheir single day record highs, so stay tuned!\n\nAnother cold front looks to drop through on Tuesday, bringing\ntemperatures back into 70s and low 80sF for the rest of the week.\n\nGiven the warm temperatures over the coming week, expect strong \nafternoon mixing to produce breezy to locally windy conditions at \ntimes during the warmest part of each afternoon. \n\nThe combination of warm, dry, and breezy conditions will bring\nperiods of elevated fire weather conditions through next week.\nWill need to use extra caution to prevent grass fires until\na cooler and wetter weather pattern develops.\n\nMatos/Archer",
